{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And it shall be.</b> Even though streams grow great on the way, there shall be there a cleared path, a highway." "<b>And the way of holiness.</b> Because of their return to Jerusalem." "<b>Shall not pass over it.</b> Every impure nation, even though the way was theirs, they shall fear to pass over it, and they shall walk in the cleared path of the redeemed. And furthermore, whoever walks on the way, and fools — they shall not know him. <b>They shall not err</b>, for it shall be a cleared path."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {2 "The syntax of ואוילים שלא ידעוהו is difficult; translated hyper-literally. The phrase may be corrupt or elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:46.908621661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}